Guided Exercise: Application Autoscaling
Objective
•	Deploy an application.
•	Manually scale the deployment up and down.
•	Set CPU resource requests and limits.
•	Configure a Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) to automatically scale the deployment under load.
•	Observe autoscaling behavior during simulated CPU load.
________________________________________
2. Lab Setup
lab start reliability-autoscaling
oc login -u developer -p developer https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
oc project reliability-autoscaling
•	This ensures the cluster is ready and the reliability-autoscaling project exists.
________________________________________
3. Deploy the Application
oc apply -f ~/DO180/labs/reliability-autoscaling/loadtest.yml
watch oc get pods
•	Deployment uses the loadtest:v1.0 image.
•	Pod exposes a CPU-intensive endpoint at /api/loadtest/v1/cpu/1.
•	Pod initially does not define CPU resource requests, which prevents HPA from working.
________________________________________
4. Attempt HPA Before Requests
oc autoscale deployment/loadtest --min 2 --max 20 --cpu-percent 50
oc get hpa loadtest
oc describe hpa loadtest
•	TARGETS shows <unknown> because CPU requests are missing.
•	Event shows: failed to get cpu utilization: missing request for cpu.
•	Solution: define CPU requests/limits in the deployment YAML.
________________________________________
5. Add CPU Requests & Limits
Edit loadtest.yml:
resources:
  requests:
    cpu: 25m   # pod needs 25 millicores to operate
  limits:
    cpu: 100m  # max CPU the pod can consume
Redeploy:
oc apply -f ~/DO180/labs/reliability-autoscaling/loadtest.yml
watch oc get pods
________________________________________
6. Manual Scaling
•	Scale up to 5 pods:
oc scale deployment/loadtest --replicas 5
watch oc get pods
•	Scale down to 1 pod:
oc scale deployment/loadtest --replicas 1
watch oc get pods
________________________________________
7. Create Horizontal Pod Autoscaler
oc autoscale deployment/loadtest --min 2 --max 20 --cpu-percent 50
watch oc get hpa loadtest
•	Initially, HPA ensures minimum 2 replicas.
•	After the deployment has CPU requests defined, TARGETS will show current CPU usage.
________________________________________
8. Simulate Load
1.	Get application route:
oc get route loadtest
2.	Send CPU-intensive requests:
curl loadtest-reliability-autoscaling.apps.ocp4.example.com/api/loadtest/v1/cpu/1
•	Multiple requests may be needed to trigger autoscaler.
•	HPA scales up pods according to CPU usage.
•	HPA scales down more slowly, often taking several minutes after CPU load decreases.
________________________________________
9. Monitor Autoscaling
•	Watch HPA status and pod metrics:
watch oc get hpa loadtest
watch oc get pods
•	Observe replicas increase when CPU > target, decrease when CPU < target.
________________________________________
10. Lab Cleanup
lab finish reliability-autoscaling
________________________________________
Key Notes
•	Resource requests are mandatory for CPU-based HPA. Without them, HPA cannot calculate utilization.
•	Limits prevent a pod from consuming too much CPU or memory.
•	HPA is reactive; scaling up is faster than scaling down.
•	Load testing helps verify HPA behavior.



